course: dictionary
lesson: 9788
title: Survival and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Survival means staying alive, especially in danger or a hard situation. It can also mean continuing to exist, as in «the survival of a species». The words around the word tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Jungle and survival shows have doctors, crews and safety rules behind the camera, even when the people look all alone.» The clues are «doctors, crews and safety rules» and «even when the people look all alone». So survival here means staying alive in a hard, pretend-dangerous situation, while real people keep everyone safe.
explain: «Every tank holds a different survival trick: a stick insect sways like a twig.» The word trick tells you survival means a way of staying safe, and sways like a twig tells you the trick is about hiding. Always check: if you swap in your meaning, does the sentence still make sense?
fact: Survival is an uncountable noun: you say survival, not a survival, unless you mean a thing left from the past.
fact: «Survival» means staying alive, especially in danger or a hard situation.
fact: «Survival» can also mean continuing to exist, like the survival of a species or a business.
fact: «Survival skills» are skills such as finding shelter, water and help.
fact: «Survival of the fittest» is linked to evolution: animals best suited to their habitat survive and have young.
exercise: «Every tank holds a different survival trick: a stick insect sways like a twig.» What does survival trick mean here? | A loud noise made to scare visitors | A pet that likes to swim | A cleaning job for the glass tank | *A way of staying safe and hidden
exercise: Which clue in «Jungle and survival shows have doctors, crews and safety rules behind the camera» tells you real people are kept safe? | *doctors, crews and safety rules | shows | jungle | camera
exercise: Which meaning fits «the survival of a species»? | A thing left from long ago | *Continuing to exist | A kind of sports shoe | Staying alive in a fire
test: «Survival» can mean something left from the past. Which meaning is this? | *Something that still exists from long ago | Continuing to exist as a business | Staying alive in danger | A loud, angry shout
test: In science, «survival of the fittest» means | Animals must stay in the same place forever | Fish swim faster than birds | A race for the strongest runner | *Animals best suited to their habitat survive and have young
exam: Which phrase would a safety lesson use for finding shelter, water and help in the wild? | survival trick, meaning a stick insect | survival shows | survival of the fittest | *survival skills
